.TH wmsetbg 1 "April 2015"
.SH NAME
wmsetbg \- sets the background on the X11 display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmsetbg
.RI [ \-display " display]"
.RI [ \-\-update-domain " domain|" \-\-update-wmaker ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ image ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmsetbg
reads the specified
.I image
(in any format supported by the
.I WRaster
library) and puts it on the root window. It can
either scale the image or tile it to make it fit the root
window. Window Maker uses this command internally to set the root
window image on start up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c | \-b | \--color " \fIcolor\fP"
the specified \fIcolor\fP is used as the background color, both for the
\fIsolid_color\fP mode and as the letterbox fill behind a centered or
\fIfit\fP image. You can specify colors using their X11 names or as an
RGB triplet (either as "rgb:RR/GG/BB" or "#RRGGBB"). \fB\-\-back\-color\fP
is accepted as a deprecated alias.
.TP
.BR \-\-center | \-e
centers the \fIimage\fP in the screen
.TP
.BR \-display " \fIdisplay\fP"
connect to the X \fIdisplay\fP
.TP
.BR \-\-dynamic-color [=Auto|Light|Dark]
derive a UI palette (titlebar, menu, icon, and frame colors) from the
wallpaper and write it to the WindowMaker domain database, so the next
reconfigure applies the derived colors. The optional \fIMODE\fP selects
the framing ladder direction: \fBAuto\fP (default) picks light or dark
based on the average swatch luminance, \fBLight\fP and \fBDark\fP force
the direction. The derived colors overwrite the user's theme keys. A
subsequent wallpaper change re\-derives, and omitting the flag leaves the
user's values untouched.
.TP
.BR \-\-fillscale | \-f
scales the specified \fIimage\fP to fill screen while preserving aspect ratio
.TP
.BR \-\-help | \-h
print a help message with the list of options
.TP
.BR \-\-maxscale | \-a
scales the specified \fIimage\fP to fit inside the screen preserving its aspect ratio
.TP
.BR \-\-mode | \-m " \fImode\fP"
set the background mode: \fItile\fP, \fIcenter\fP, \fIscale\fP, \fIfit\fP,
\fIfill\fP, or \fIsolid_color\fP. The short flags \fB\-t\fP, \fB\-e\fP,
\fB\-s\fP, \fB\-a\fP and \fB\-f\fP are aliases for \fItile\fP, \fIcenter\fP,
\fIscale\fP, \fIfit\fP and \fIfill\fP respectively. \fIsolid_color\fP
paints the \fIcolor\fP without an image.
.TP
.BR \-\-output | \-o " \fIname\fP"
assign the following \fIimage\fP, \fImode\fP and \fIcolor\fP arguments to
a specific output. May be given more than once. Outputs not named on the
command line inherit the default spec gathered before the first
\fB\-\-output\fP.
.TP
.BR \-\-parse | \-p " \fItexture\fP"
parses the specified \fItexture\fP as a \fIproplist style texture\fP
.TP
.BR \-\-scale | \-s
scales the specified \fIimage\fP to fill the screen (default)
.TP
.BR \-\-smooth | \-S
use a smooth scaling algorithm when resizing \fIimage\fP
.TP
.BR \-\-stretch\-all | \-X
stretch one image across all heads instead of applying it per-output.
\fB\-\-xinerama\fP is accepted as a deprecated alias.
.TP
.BR \-\-tile | \-t
tiles the specified \fIimage\fP
.TP
.BR \-\-update\-domain | \-D " \fIdomain\fP"
updates the specified \fIdomain\fP database
.TP
.BR \-\-update\-wmaker | \-u
updates the Window Maker defaults database
.TP
.BR \-\-version | \-v
print the version of Window Maker from which the program comes
.TP
.BR \-\-workspace | \-w " \fIworkspace\fP"
update background only for the specified \fIworkspace\fP
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmaker (1)
